| `models.credential_env.<adapter>` | list of strings | `claude-code-headless` gets `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` and `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`; `openai-compatible` gets `OPENAI_API_KEY` | an adapter mapped to the credential variables it may use | `scripts/child_env.py` (`build_child_env(credentials_for=...)`, `load_policy`); `models/openai_compatible.py`; `evals/_run.py`; check_X | For an adapter that starts a process, adds variables to that adapter's child only; an adapter not listed gets the base allowlist. For `openai-compatible`, which sends the credential itself, lists the only names its `api_key_env` argument accepts. A live eval run replaces each listed variable's value with `<hidden>` in its report's case details. | every child: `child_env.names`; where the credential may be sent: `models.allowed_hosts` | always |
